xrepl> // Every % command, including the ways they go wrong.
xrepl> %help
%help             list xrepl %commands
%undo [N]         undo the previous N inputs (default 1)
%lib <path>       link a dynamic library
%quit             exit xrepl
%ast [name]       AST of the last input, or of the named declaration
%ir [full]        LLVM IR of the last input (captured before it ran)
%type <expr>      static type, size and value category; the expression is not run
%inspect [expr]   fields of an object in JIT memory (no argument: the last value)
%decls            every declaration so far, grouped by input
%complete <text>  completion candidates for text, as Tab shows them
%time <input>     run an input and report parse and execute time
xrepl> %nosuch
error: Invalid % command "%nosuch", use "%help" to list commands

xrepl> %nosuch with arguments
error: Invalid % command "%nosuch with arguments", use "%help" to list commands

xrepl> %lib
error: %lib expects 1 argument: the path to a dynamic library
xrepl> %undo zero
error: usage: %undo [N]
xrepl> %undo 0
error: usage: %undo [N]
xrepl> %type
error: usage: %type <expression>
xrepl> %ast nosuch
error: no declaration named 'nosuch'
xrepl> %ir bogus
error: usage: %ir [full]
xrepl> %time
error: usage: %time <C++ input>
xrepl> %time %help
error: usage: %time <C++ input>
xrepl> %inspect nosuch.field
In file included from <<< inputs >>>:1:
input_line_2:1:30: error: use of undeclared identifier 'nosuch'
    1 | using __xrepl_ty = decltype((nosuch.field));
      |                              ^~~~~~
error: Parsing failed.
xrepl> %quit
